.TH OMACHAT-CTL 1 "2026-08-31" "OmaChat 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
omachat-ctl \- control an OmaChat daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachat-ctl
[\fB--socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [--json]
Show daemon, relay, storage, join, outbox, and local account state, including
account and device IDs, configured handle and display name, binding revision,
and registry state. A configured handle is reported as local-only; it is not a
claim that a live global registry has accepted the handle.
.TP
.B fingerprint
Print the stable Noise fingerprint.
.TP
.B fingerprint --qr
Render the same fingerprint as an ANSI QR code using qrencode.
.TP
.B join GEOHASH
Join a public geohash conversation.
.TP
.B leave GEOHASH
Leave a public geohash conversation.
.TP
.B send CONVERSATION TEXT
Queue a public or private message. A room conversation is addressed as
\fBroom:\fIRELAY_PUBKEY\fB:\fIGROUP\fR, as reported by \fBrooms\fR.
.TP
.B join-room RELAY GROUP [--invite CODE]
Subscribe to a NIP-29 room on a configured room relay and send a join request.
The relay's policy, not the daemon, decides membership; the response reports
whether the relay accepted the request.
.TP
.B leave-room RELAY GROUP
Send a leave request and unsubscribe from the room.
.TP
.B rooms [--json]
Describe every configured room relay: its verified signing identity, how that
identity was obtained, connection state, and the joined rooms with their
relay-published metadata.
.TP
.B panic --confirm ERASE
Cryptographically erase local state and stop the daemon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 usage; 3 connection; 4 protocol/remote error; 5 timeout.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omachat (1),
.BR omachatd (8)
